9. Algorithm
Algorithm for Insertion
1.Start from the root.
2.If the root is empty, create a new node.
3.Compare the new Patient ID with the current node.
4.If smaller, move to the left subtree.
5.If greater, move to the right subtree.
6.Repeat until an empty position is found and insert the node.
Algorithm for Searching
7.Start at the root.
8.Compare the required Patient ID with the current node.
9.If equal, the patient is found.
10.If smaller, move to the left subtree.
11.If greater, move to the right subtree.
12.If the node becomes None, the patient is not found.
Algorithm for Deletion
13.Search for the required Patient ID.
14.If the node is a leaf, remove it.
15.If it has one child, replace it with its child.
16.If it has two children, find the inorder successor.
17.Replace the node value with the successor value.
18.Delete the successor node.
Algorithm for Level-wise Traversal
19.Create an empty queue.
20.Insert the root into the queue.
21.Remove one node from the queue and display its Patient ID.
22.Insert its left child, if present.
23.Insert its right child, if present.
24.Repeat until the queue becomes empty.
